# Data and build artefacts never belong in the repo. The evidence plane grows
# to tens of gigabytes and lives at $MENDELEA_DATA_DIR (default ~/mendelea-data),
# deliberately outside any synced folder.
#
# This catches `mendelea-public.duckdb` too, and that is deliberate rather
# than incidental: at ~60 MB it would push (GitHub warns over 50 MB and
# refuses over 100), but git stores every version of a binary in full and
# forever, so each regeneration would add another 60 MB to a history that can
# never be pruned without rewriting it. It is also derived -- one command from
# the warehouse, which is one command from the snapshots.
#
# Back it up as a GitHub Release asset instead (2 GB per file, no effect on
# clone size, and a URL that CI and a Dockerfile can fetch):
#
#   gh release create data-$(date +%Y-%m-%d) mendelea-public.duckdb \
#       --title "Public demo warehouse" --notes "31-gene panel, 8 releases"
#
# The snapshots under $MENDELEA_DATA_DIR/evidence are the ones actually worth
# archiving: they are the system of record, they are content-addressed, and
# re-ingesting produces different bytes now that DuckDB writes them. See the
# backup section of README.md.
*.duckdb
*.duckdb.wal
*.parquet
*.parquet.partial
*.manifest.json

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# Editors / OS
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# The bundled gene coordinate cache IS tracked on purpose -- it lets a fresh
# clone ingest the standard panels with no external lookup.
!panels/gene_regions.json
